      "id": "AR-ING-06-2026-W04-daily-routines-005",
      "statement": "Where does an adverb of frequency (like \"always\") go with the verb \"to be\"?",
      "context": "Grammar rule for adverbs with the verb \"to be\".",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "Before the verb \"to be\".",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrect."
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "After the verb \"to be\".",
          "is_correct": true,
          "feedback": "Correct. Example: \"I am always happy.\""
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "At the end of the sentence.",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrect."
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "At the beginning.",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrect."
        }
      ],
      "correct_answer": "B",
      "explanation": "Con el verbo \"to be\", los adverbios de frecuencia se colocan después del verbo.\n\n---",
